  "text": {
    "intro": "The Vance Municipal Archive was reorganised in 1974 by somebody who has since left no forwarding address.\nFive archivists are involved. Determine each archivist's shelf, decade and condition.\n- **Archivist**: Dr Mwangi, Ms Castellano, Dr Lindqvist, Mr Ravensworth and Ms Okafor.\n- **Shelf** (listed from lower to higher): the bottom shelf, the second shelf, the third shelf, the fourth shelf and the fifth shelf.\n- **Decade**: the 1890s, the 1970s, the 1910s, the 1950s and the 1830s.\n- **Condition**: immaculate, water-damaged, fire-scorched, over-repaired with tape and foxed.\nEvery archivist has a different shelf, decade and condition, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "Ms Castellano and the bottom shelf are exactly four shelves apart in shelf order. The archivist who covers the 1890s does not file on the bottom shelf.",
      "The archivist who describes theirs as water-damaged and the bottom shelf are exactly one shelf apart in shelf order, in one direction or the other.",
      "The archivist who describes theirs as foxed falls somewhere between Dr Lindqvist and Dr Mwangi in shelf order.",
      "The archivist who covers the 1970s is exactly one shelf lower than the archivist who describes theirs as fire-scorched, with no shelf in between.",
      "Dr Lindqvist is exactly one shelf lower than the archivist who describes theirs as over-repaired with tape, with no shelf in between.",
      "Dr Lindqvist is exactly one shelf lower than the archivist who covers the 1910s, with no shelf in between.",
      "Ms Okafor and the archivist who covers the 1970s are exactly one shelf apart in shelf order, in one direction or the other.",
      "The archivist who describes theirs as water-damaged is lower than the archivist who covers the 1830s in shelf order."
    ]
